# Citation metadata for Open Docking.
#
# `contact` is intentionally absent: add one with a monitored address before
# publishing so that citation requests have somewhere to go.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Open Docking"
abstract: >-
  A molecular docking engine written as a pure-safe Rust core with a Python
  chemistry front end and an interactive 3-D workbench. The engine reproduces
  the form of the AutoDock Vina empirical scoring function with analytic
  first-order gradients, precalculated affinity maps on a four-slot grid, an
  iterated local search with optional island-model LGA, and an optional
  GPU batch-scoring path. Distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later.
type: software
